source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-23
observed: A link's title parameter keeps its `|` inside the cell.
-- input.jira --
||h1||h2||
|[x|http://x|title]|c|
-- rendered.html --
<div class='table-wrap'>
<table class='confluenceTable'><tbody>
<tr>
<th class='confluenceTh'>h1</th>
<th class='confluenceTh'>h2</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class='confluenceTd'><a href="http://x" title="title" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">x</a></td>
<td class='confluenceTd'>c</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
</div>
-- want.md --
| h1 | h2 |
| --- | --- |
| [x](http://x\|title) | c |
-- warnings.json --
[]
